# Force LF for files Claude Code parses at any nesting depth, and for the
# root instruction files it reads on startup. Without this, a checkout on a
# host with core.autocrlf=true (e.g. GitHub's windows-latest runners) can
# silently rewrite these to CRLF even though the committed blob is LF —
# CRLF line endings make Claude Code silently ignore these files, and CRLF
# in a SKILL.md fails tests/test_skill_frontmatter.py's LF guard for reasons
# unrelated to content correctness.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no blanket `* text=auto` rule that would renormalize
# the whole repo.
**/SKILL.md text eol=lf
.claude/** text eol=lf
/CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
/AGENTS.md text eol=lf
